# What `railway up` leaves out (Moses, 27 Oct 2026: the whole repository, 88 MB, kept failing to upload).
# Only the game server goes up. It reads, and so nothing here may leave out:
#   package.json, package-lock.json   (Railway installs and starts the server from them)
#   src/                              (all of it: /health's code fingerprint is a hash of every src/**/*.js)
#   scripts/                          (small; src/report uses scripts/race-fingerprints.js)
#   docs/database_schema.sql, docs/data_updates/   (applied at every start, src/db/migrate.js)
#   client/src/shared/                (the settings the server shares with the website: economy.json,
#                                      company.json, push.json, nameFilter.js, marbles/catalog.json, …)
# Everything below is the website, the apps, pictures, music, review sheets, measurements and docs.
# Plain paths from the top folder only (a leading "/"; no "!" re-includes), so every ignore-file reader treats it the same.
# Adding a folder the server reads? Check it isn't listed here (docs/05-runbook.md, "Deploying").

